 // the default keyboard and gamepad mapping, which stays on except for a device the file
 // names.
 //
+// Any game controller SDL knows (Xbox, DualShock/DualSense, Switch Pro and Joy-Con, the
+// GameCube adapter, ...), by its standard name rather than a device and a number:
+//   pad <button>                  a b x y back guide start leftstick rightstick
+//                                 leftshoulder rightshoulder dpup dpdown dpleft dpright
+//                                 misc1 paddle1 paddle2 paddle3 paddle4 touchpad
+//                                 (a/b/x/y are positions: a is the bottom face button)
+//   pad <axis>  / pad <axis>+|-   leftx lefty rightx righty lefttrigger righttrigger
+//                                 (y axes are + downwards, as SDL has them)
+//   pad2 <...>                    only the second controller (pad1, pad3, ...); `pad`
+//                                 alone reads every controller connected.
+// Stick axes get a dead zone of 0.12 unless the line gives one.
+//
+// The mouse:
+//   mouse left|right|middle|x1|x2
+//   mouse wheelup|wheeldown       pressed for the poll after a notch
+//   mouse x / mouse y (+|-)       relative motion: with gain 1, 50 pixels in one poll is
+//                                 full deflection. Binding either captures the pointer
+//                                 (click in the window to capture, mouse_release_key to
+//                                 let go, F1 by default).
+//
+// Whole-file settings:
+//   defaults = off                no built-in keyboard/gamepad layout: only this file
+//   quit_key = <key>|none         the key that closes the program (Escape by default)
+//   mouse_release_key = <key>     toggles mouse capture (F1 by default)
+//
 // --list-controls runs input_map_probe() instead of the game: it prints the devices and,
 // for each control pressed or moved, the source to paste into the file.
